# ---- 720 Technology Applications Independent Study (Independent Study I) ----
H("720.d.1.A",3,"In an independent study course, a student draws on what they already know to design a new app for tracking recycling. This applies existing knowledge to promote:","creativity in designing a new technology product",["copying a finished product","avoiding all planning","deleting old files"],"Prior knowledge fuels new design ideas.")
H("720.d.1.A",4,"Which habit best promotes creativity when designing a new technology product?","Combining known skills in new ways to meet a real need",["Repeating the same design every time","Waiting for someone to assign ideas","Avoiding any research"],"Creativity builds on knowledge and need.")
H("720.d.1.B",3,"An independent study student keeps a calendar of milestones and checks industry news for new tools. This is tracking:","trends and timelines for the project",["only lunch times","only desk locations","only passwords"],"Timelines and trends guide the project.")
H("720.d.1.B",4,"Reviewing and evaluating a project's progress against its timeline at set intervals helps a student to:","catch delays early and adjust the plan",["avoid all deadlines","hide problems","skip the final product"],"Regular reviews keep a study on track.")
H("720.d.1.C",3,"A student saves dated screenshots, a progress log and drafts in a shared folder. This is:","electronic documentation of project progress",["a hardware repair","a license purchase","a network outage"],"Documentation shows the project's growth.")
H("720.d.1.C",4,"A good electronic progress record for an independent study includes:","dates, work completed and next steps",["only a title","unrelated jokes","blank pages"],"Complete records show real progress.")
H("720.d.1.D",3,"A student shows an early prototype to a teacher and an industry mentor and asks what to improve. This is:","seeking input from peers and professionals",["ignoring feedback","hiding the work","quitting the study"],"Feedback shapes technology decisions.")
H("720.d.1.D",4,"When a mentor suggests a change that conflicts with the student's plan, a mature response is to:","consider the input and decide how to respond",["reject it automatically","ignore the mentor","argue until the mentor leaves"],"Thoughtful responses to input improve outcomes.")
H("720.d.1.E",3,"After a review, a student fixes the problems found and then moves on to the next phase. This is:","making revisions and proceeding to the next stage",["restarting forever","dropping the project","hiding the problems"],"Revise, then advance.")
H("720.d.1.E",4,"A student whose test results show the product meets every requirement should:","proceed to the next stage of study",["revise everything again","delete the product","restart from scratch"],"If criteria are met, move on.")
H("720.d.1.F",3,"In a project report, a student correctly uses terms such as bandwidth, interface and database. This is:","using appropriate technology terminology",["using slang only","avoiding detail","writing in code only"],"Precise terms show understanding.")
H("720.d.1.F",4,"Using accurate technology terms in an independent study helps the student to:","communicate clearly with professionals",["confuse the audience","avoid questions","shorten the day"],"Shared vocabulary improves communication.")
H("720.d.1.G",3,"A student builds a tool that combines several apps in a way no tutorial shows. This reflects:","advanced creativity and innovation in technology applications",["a routine copy","a simple restart","a deleted file"],"Innovation goes beyond the standard.")
H("720.d.1.G",4,"Which project shows advanced innovation rather than routine use?","Designing a new workflow that automates a repeated school task",["Typing a document","Opening a browser","Printing a page"],"Innovation solves problems in new ways.")
H("720.d.1.H",3,"A student's program crashes, so they test pieces separately and ask a mentor about the error. This is:","identifying and solving a problem with peer and professional input",["avoiding the problem","blaming the computer","deleting the program"],"Problem solving can use outside help.")
