H("721.d.3.B",4,"Adding a minus sign before a word in a search tells the engine to:","exclude results containing that word",["ignore the whole search","delete the page","print results"],"Operators narrow results.")
H("721.d.3.C",3,"A student asks, \"Does a darker interface theme reduce eye strain in night use?\" This is:","a question tied to a selected problem",["a conclusion","a citation","a title page"],"Questions drive research.")
H("721.d.3.C",4,"A well-formed hypothesis for the study must be:","testable and related to the problem",["unprovable","unrelated","already proven"],"Testability is essential.")
H("721.d.3.D",3,"For each fact in her report, Dana records where it came from. She is:","acquiring information with source citations",["hiding sources","guessing","copying"],"Source records support credibility.")
H("721.d.3.D",4,"Including accurate citations in a research product shows the student:","respects the work of other authors",["copied everything","has no sources","avoided research"],"Citing gives credit.")
H("721.d.3.E",3,"A student creates a podcast, a slideshow, a spreadsheet and a PDF for one project. These show use of:","a variety of file formats",["a single format","no formats","only text"],"Projects often use many formats.")
H("721.d.3.E",4,"When choosing a format for a report to be read on any device, the best option is a:","widely supported, cross-platform format",["rare proprietary format","hidden format","corrupted file"],"Common formats open anywhere.")
H("721.d.4.A",3,"Before citing a statistic, a student confirms the publisher's reputation and checks whether other reliable sources agree. This is:","evaluating the accuracy of accessed information",["accepting any claim","ignoring errors","skipping checks"],"Accuracy requires verification.")
H("721.d.4.A",4,"A claim appears on one anonymous blog and nowhere else. The student should:","treat it with caution and look for corroboration",["cite it as fact","copy it","ignore all other sources"],"Corroborate uncertain claims.")
H("721.d.4.B",3,"A student sets research questions, searches multiple databases, compares results and records the process. This is:","conducting systematic research",["random browsing","guessing","skipping documentation"],"Systematic research is planned and recorded.")
H("721.d.4.B",4,"The main value of recording search terms and databases used is that it:","lets others repeat and verify the research",["wastes time","hides the method","removes accuracy"],"Records support verification.")
H("721.d.4.C",3,"Faced with a failed prototype, Lena sketches three alternative designs and tests each. She is showing:","creative thinking and problem-solving skills",["avoidance","quitting","copying"],"Exploring alternatives builds solutions.")
H("721.d.4.C",4,"A creative problem solver whose approach fails tends to:","analyze why and try a different approach",["repeat the same step","give up","blame tools"],"Analysis and adaptation are central.")
H("721.d.4.D",3,"A student gathers field data on a tablet that syncs to a shared spreadsheet and a project board. This integrates:","network, mobile access and productivity tools",["only paper tools","unrelated tools","no tools"],"Integrated tools streamline work.")
H("721.d.4.D",4,"Which setup best integrates mobile access with productivity tools for team data entry?","A phone form that writes to a shared spreadsheet",["A paper log","A voicemail","A printed chart"],"Mobile forms feed shared files.")
H("721.d.4.E",3,"A student includes real statistics from a math unit and diagrams from science in the study's final product. This is:","using enriched curricular content in creating products",["avoiding content","using blank charts","ignoring data"],"Cross-curricular content enriches products.")
H("721.d.4.E",4,"Using accurate content from other classes in a technology product helps by:","making the product more informative and credible",["making it empty","hiding the topic","lowering quality"],"Content adds depth.")
H("721.d.4.F",3,"From several electronic surveys, a student builds one new data set and writes new insights. This is:","synthesizing and generating new information from gathered data",["copying one survey","deleting data","hiding results"],"Synthesis produces new insight.")
H("721.d.4.F",4,"True synthesis of electronic data requires:","combining sources and drawing original conclusions",["repeating one source","summarizing nothing","skipping analysis"],"New information comes from combining data.")
H("721.d.4.G",3,"To configure a router, a student follows the manufacturer's setup guide step by step. This is:","reading and using technical documentation",["guessing","ignoring directions","skipping steps"],"Technical manuals guide tasks.")
H("721.d.4.G",4,"A good habit when using technical documentation is to:","read warnings and notes before starting the steps",["skip the warnings","read only the index","ignore diagrams"],"Warnings prevent mistakes.")
H("721.d.4.H",3,"A student drafts a short how-to for new users of her project app, written at a beginner level. This is:","simple technical documentation written for the audience",["a poem","a cartoon","a private note"],"Write for the reader.")
H("721.d.4.H",4,"Technical documentation for non-experts should include:","plain steps and examples",["unexplained jargon","no instructions","only diagrams without labels"],"Clarity serves the audience.")
H("721.d.5.A",3,"A class discussion covers why reposting a stranger's artwork without permission may violate copyright and why sharing someone's private data can harm them. The topics are:","intellectual property, privacy and information sharing",["font styles","paper sizes","cable colors"],"IP and privacy are core ethics topics.")
H("721.d.5.A",4,"Which is a privacy concern when posting online?","Revealing someone's address or photos without consent",["Picking a font","Choosing a page title","Setting the volume"],"Privacy requires consent.")
H("721.d.5.B",3,"Sam obtains permission before using a dataset and lists the owner in the credits. This models:","ethical acquisition and use of digital information",["piracy","hacking","spam"],"Permission and credit are ethical practices.")
H("721.d.5.B",4,"A student who downloads a licensed image for free from the official site's free section and credits the author is:","using digital information ethically",["stealing","hacking","plagiarizing"],"Use of free-licensed content with credit is ethical.")
H("721.d.5.C",3,"A video editor uses only clips whose license allows remixing and adds credits. This shows:","respect for intellectual property when editing media",["disrespect for rights","avoiding credit","copying"],"Respect rights and credit creators.")
H("721.d.5.C",4,"Before changing a copyrighted audio track for a project, a student should:","confirm the license allows modification",["assume it's free","remove the credit","hide the source"],"Check license terms.")
H("721.d.5.D",3,"A student follows the lab's acceptable-use rules, avoids unlicensed software and treats shared devices carefully. This is:","responsible use of software and etiquette",["reckless behavior","a policy breach","a data leak"],"Responsible use follows the rules.")
H("721.d.5.D",4,"A student who understands acceptable-use policies is more likely to:","avoid actions that could cause harm or lose access",["break rules","damage equipment","share passwords"],"Policy knowledge prevents problems.")
H("721.d.5.E",3,"Regularly updating software and using a password manager are:","information security best practices",["bad habits","risky shortcuts","wasted effort"],"Updates and managers protect data.")
H("721.d.5.E",4,"A phishing email tries to trick the user into revealing a login. Best practice is to:","avoid clicking and report the message",["reply with the password","click quickly","forward to friends"],"Reporting prevents harm.")
H("721.d.5.F",3,"A student stores manuals, setup guides and notes for every tool used in the project in an organized library. This is:","developing and maintaining a technical documentation library",["deleting files","losing notes","hiding references"],"Libraries support reuse.")
H("721.d.5.F",4,"Keeping documents in a library with clear names and categories means the student can:","find reference material quickly later",["never find anything","waste space","avoid documentation"],"Organization saves time.")
H("721.d.5.G",3,"A report examines how automation changed jobs and what ethical questions it raised. It investigates:","technology's social and ethical ramifications",["hardware prices","cable colors","screen sizes"],"Technology reshapes society.")
H("721.d.5.G",4,"A social effect of facial recognition technology is:","debate over privacy and fairness",["no effect","less data","fewer cameras"],"New tech raises ethical issues.")
H("721.d.6.A",3,"A student correctly operates a scanner, tablet and stylus, and organizes files within the OS. This demonstrates:","appropriate use of input devices and operating systems",["no skill","guessing","avoiding the computer"],"Technical skills underpin the study.")
H("721.d.6.A",4,"Which is an appropriate use of an operating system for project work?","Creating a folder structure and backing up files",["Saving everything in one unnamed folder","Deleting system files","Disabling updates permanently"],"Good file management protects work.")
H("721.d.6.B",3,"A student chooses a video editor for the demo and a database program for survey data. This is:","selecting the right digital tools",["random picking","wasted effort","copying"],"Match tools to tasks.")
H("721.d.6.B",4,"Before acquiring new software for a project, the student should check:","features, cost and license terms",["only the logo","only the box","only the color"],"Evaluate tools before adopting them.")
H("721.d.6.C",3,"A project file will not open on a classmate's different operating system, so the student exports it in a shared format. This addresses:","a compatibility issue across platforms",["a color issue","a font issue","a paper issue"],"Export to a common format fixes it.")
H("721.d.6.C",4,"To prevent compatibility problems when sharing, a student should:","test files on the target platform before delivery",["send without testing","rename files randomly","hide the files"],"Test before delivery.")
H("721.d.6.D",3,"A student uses a consistent naming pattern such as team_project_draft1 for all files. This is:","using appropriate naming conventions",["random naming","no naming","blank names"],"Consistent names aid organization.")
H("721.d.6.D",4,"Naming conventions and correct technology terms in project files help a team to:","avoid confusion and find the right version",["lose files","duplicate work","miss deadlines"],"Consistency prevents errors.")

B.balance()
